  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city's historic center is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The area is characterized by its narrow streets, medieval architecture, and lively atmosphere. Visitors can explore the many museums, art galleries, and historical landmarks, such as the Cathedral of St. Mary and the City Hall. In addition to its cultural attractions, the city also boasts a thriving food scene, with numerous restaurants serving traditional cuisine.\n\nHowever, some critics argue that the historic center has become too commercialized, with souvenir shops and tourist traps dominating the streets. Others claim that the area is not well-maintained, with litter and graffiti evident in many areas. Despite these concerns, the city's authorities are working to strike a balance between preserving the area's historical charm and catering to the needs of tourists.\n\nAs a result of its rich history and cultural significance, the historic center attracts millions of visitors each year. While some may view this as a positive aspect, others see it as a threat to the area's authenticity. The debate surrounding the city's historic center is ongoing, with different stakeholders presenting their perspectives on how to preserve and promote this unique destination.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main reason why tourists visit the city's historic center?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To explore its natural beauty\", \"To experience its rich cultural heritage\", \"To shop for souvenirs\", \"To enjoy its nightlife\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To experience its rich cultural heritage\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is a common criticism of the historic center?\",\n      \"options\": [\"That it is too crowded\", \"That it has become too commercialized\", \"That it lacks historical significance\", \"That it is not well-maintained\"],\n      \"answer\": \"That it has become too commercialized\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the author imply about the city's authorities?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They are ineffective in maintaining the area\", \"They are working to strike a balance between preservation and tourism\", \"They prioritize tourist interests over local concerns\", \"They have no plans to address the area's issues\"],\n      \"answer\": \"They are working to strike a balance between preservation and tourism\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the effect of the historic center's popularity on its authenticity?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It increases its authenticity\", \"It has no impact on its authenticity\", \"It decreases its authenticity\", \"It makes it more authentic\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It decreases its authenticity\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards the debate surrounding the historic center?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical and dismissive\", \"Neutral and objective\", \"Sympathetic and understanding\", \"Oblivious to the concerns\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Sympathetic and understanding\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
